{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact Git framing head c28f8b6bbb8a458899c3856f745759713d2435f5 on builder/git-framing-variants-20261104, tree 8dad5710, for request 0466ff4e under promise d8697d39 and review request 7691d8d2. This approval covers the two Git HTTP owners, the note and the two manifests. It claims no hosted Git or provider outcome and no cause for 64552d40.\n\nScope. Main 0455c637 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The head changes only packages/git/test/http-read.test.ts and packages/git/test/http.test.ts beside the records. Product source, dependencies and every existing case stay unchanged. The commit-message check passes for both commits. No card path changes, so no Card run applies.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Independent truth. The upload fixture writes one commit to a bare repository, takes its pack from real Git, and checks that git cat-file returns the same bytes. Node zlib checks the pack entry's kind and length. Every admitted variant must return exactly those commit bytes. The generator never calls buildPack or decodePack to build an expectation.\n- Separate grammars. The 48 upload variants are the full product of optional LF, three preamble forms, capability order, shallow-info and segmentation. Segmented responses add an empty keepalive and binary progress. The 24 receive variants cover create, update and delete, ok and ng, optional LF and one or two terminal flushes. The receive grammar names the second flush as dap's retained provider allowance from 920029d5, and a third flush refuses.\n- Single edits and request counts. Each upload fault edits one component of one baseline. Advertisement faults must refuse with no POST, and response faults with exactly one. Each receive fault must read as unknown, even when read-back matches the requested value, and every receive case makes one POST.\n- Classification. A successful report confirms only with an exact same-ref read-back. It reads as unknown with another value or another ref. A rejection keeps its refused classification.\n- The three historical controls are real. Each \"old\" string appears once in the head's source. Each reversion passes its named seed before and fails it by assertion afterwards, and the helper prints DISTINGUISHES. All six focused runs exit 0, and all four source hashes in source-identity.json equal the head's files.\n- The control helper. The retained copy differs from scripts/control.mjs on one line only: it prints the scratch path instead of deleting it.\n- History. The first focused run with 36 and 12 shortened duplicate titles, and the first inconclusive LF control, stay retained and labelled. The final owners pass 120 cases with unique titles.\n\nThe gate passed. At 10f75317, gate.exit reads exit 0. All five stages pass: kernel, 135 Node, 56 Counting, 3,711 plain with one skip, and 1,070 Native with two skips. before.json and after.json match, with a clean status and lockfile 5a717d43…. The receipt lists no owned process still present.\n\nEvidence. All 22 public files match their sizes and digests and are read-only. Both SHA256SUMS files match, no unit holds an unlisted file, and the credential scan finds no match. Both manifests name checkpoint 10f75317. The private inventories match on every file: 14 focused, 560 initial controls, 578 final controls, and 2,276 gate originals with 39 selected. All are mode 0400.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The tests vary wire framing around fixed object truth and keep the real-Git owners as the witness for actual writes.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The head changes tests only.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Two notes:\n\n- The protocol documents ground the admitted upload set. Some refusals encode dap's own strictness where protocol-v2 says nothing, for example a duplicate fetch or object-format line. The note describes them as single edits, not as protocol violations, and that wording is accurate.\n- In the receive grammar, capability order follows the LF choice, so order and LF don't